From 819a9ca9adfd833ab67fcc676eff0a7dc810cd2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] mips: jz47xx: x2600: SPL: eMMC data at the middle of
 the sample window

The SPL reads the eMMC at 25 MHz with the sample point the boot ROM
leaves in MSC0CDR, RX phase 0. On an X2600E unit with an A31M8C eMMC
every data read then fails with a data CRC error, while commands and
reads at 400 kHz work. Swept on that unit, reads are correct from RX
phase 1 to 5 (2 to 5 with the TX phase at 270 degrees).

Set RX phase 3 with tuning off, as Ingenic's soc_mmc_set_rx_phase()
does for its working clock.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
[Kiln OS: not tied to the SoC variant, it follows the eMMC part.
 Started from the eMMC, the SPL first reads at the phase the boot ROM
 left, so a board whose eMMC works there (the X2600H boards so far) is
 read exactly as before, with no phase write. Any data read that fails
 (a data CRC error, or another step: the line before says which) sets
 RX phase 3 with tuning off, logs one line and is read again; later
 reads keep that phase. Started over USB, the ROM never set the eMMC
 up, so MSC0CDR gets the ROM's eMMC value (as in the chainload test
 build) and then RX phase 3, before the first read. A read that still
 fails is tried once more from CMD0 at 400 kHz and 1 bit; if that
 works, booting goes on that way (slowly: 64 KiB reads, the phase's
 watchdog restarted before each). Each failed read logs the step
 (command busy, timeout or error; a data block or the transfer's end,
 timeout or error) with SD_INT_STATUS, SD_PRESENT_STATE and MSC0CDR,
 and spl_load_uimage() tells a read error from no image
 (djvalic/kiln-os#68).]
